A||||2||batboy||Batmobile alignment||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||05-19-2000||03:55 PM||||Got a 4 wheel alignment on my V8 Fiero today. I told them that I preferred nobody driving it but me. They said "no problem" and let me pull it into the shop and up onto the alignment rack. I shut it off and the guy exclaimed "What kind of engine you got in that thing?!?" When I told him a V8 350, everyone in the shop stopped working and wandered over to check it out. Talk about an ego trip. They even let me work on a couple minor things under the car while it was up on the rack getting aligned.<P>On the way back to work, a fairly new F-150 Ford truck reved at me while we were at the stop light. I gunned my engine back at them and we all grinned at each other. The light turned red and they floored it chirping the truck tires. The pickup was quicker than I initially thought, but I couldn't resist. I tromped down hard on the gas, pulled a couple car lengths ahead and then I shut it down (was already over the speed limit). The dang truck did a typical ricer flyby. I just smiled and waved, knowing full well they saw my bat brake lights pop on when I shut down. Oddly enough, neither guy in the truck smiled back. Hahaha, poor losers. Don't mess with the Batmobile!!!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 05-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-19-2000||06:25 PM||||I know the feeling man, I once spanked a V8 Dakota!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It was a pretty trashed though, so I'm not especially proud of that one.||||reg||1
